Subject: [PATCH] xtensa/espressif: skip a declared SIMPLE_BOOT prefix digest

Base: apache/nuttx 2b5c0de5e933281c209f954a63b99cf10c132346 (13.1.0)

The ROM-visible image ends after its RAM segments and aligned checksum.
When hash_appended is one, skip its 32-byte SHA-256 before parsing the
hidden padding and flash-mapped segments. Keep flag-zero legacy images
unchanged. This adds parsing support, not digest verification or secure boot.

The MPSC comparison consumes existing zero padding instead of moving mapped
payloads. Physical boot and target-build qualification remain separate
requirements.

diff --git a/arch/xtensa/src/common/espressif/esp_loader.c b/arch/xtensa/src/common/espressif/esp_loader.c
--- a/arch/xtensa/src/common/espressif/esp_loader.c
+++ b/arch/xtensa/src/common/espressif/esp_loader.c
@@ -252,6 +252,16 @@
       if (ram_segments == image_header.segment_count && !padding_checksum)
         {
           offset += (CHECKSUM_ALIGN - 1) - (offset % CHECKSUM_ALIGN) + 1;
+
+          /* A declared SHA-256 follows the ROM-visible checksum.  It is not
+           * a segment header.  Legacy SIMPLE_BOOT images omit this digest.
+           */
+
+          if (image_header.hash_appended == 1)
+            {
+              offset += 32;
+            }
+
           padding_checksum = true;
         }
     }
